On Wednesday, April 1, 2015 at 8:23:11 AM UTC-4, Allen B. Riddell wrote:
> If it's guaranteed to be contiguous then vector<double> is certainly
> better.
>
> Maybe I'm remembering something different -- perhaps it was
> vector<vector<double>> that I couldn't seamlessly deal with in NumPy.

vector became contiguous by standard with the 03 standard:

http://stackoverflow.com/questions/849168/are-stdvector-elements-guaranteed-to-be-contiguous

I'm pretty sure vector<vector<double>> would not be contiguous, but at that point using Eigen types seems easier. Rcpp (well, RcppEigen) will let rstan handle Eigen matrices easily, they are contiguous, and you can get a pointer to the Eigen matrix data array (and go the double* route) for Python.

Krzysztof

