PyStan currently doesn't wrap Eigen and there's no equivalent for
RcppEigen. If vector<double> is contiguous it can be converted into a
NumPy array without a copy.

Here's the C++ FAQ entry on the topic:

https://isocpp.org/wiki/faq/containers#vector-is-contiguous

It says the proper way to access the memory is via `vec.data()`.

Best,

Allen

