Firstly, we’re talking about moving data from Stan into the interfaces
so the important part is that we can expose the underlying contiguous
memory so that the interfaces can do what they need to do.

Going the other way we can play a few tricks — C++11 adds a bunch
of direct-data manipulation methods to the STL library so I don’t think
it will require trying to create an std::vector wrapper.

